new file mode 100644
index 0000000..37413cf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROLLBACK_1.1.0.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Rollback plan: 1.1.0 -> 1.0.0
+
+1.1.0 has no schema migration, so databases are compatible with both versions and no data
+restore is needed.
+
+1. Redeploy the 1.0.0 tag/artifact (or `git revert` the release commit and the delete fix).
+2. Confirm `taskboard.__version__ == "1.0.0"` and run `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`.
+3. Smoke test: `add`, `list`, `complete` for one owner against the existing database file.
+4. Note: rolling back re-opens the cross-owner `delete()` gap. Restrict access to delete
+   until a fixed release ships.
+
+Trigger: any failing delete/complete behavior, or data loss reports after upgrade.
+Before upgrading, back up SQLite files (`cp tasks.db tasks.db.bak-1.0.0`).
